meta {
  name: install a set of catalogue skills
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/skills/install-set
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "skills": [
      "superpowers/brainstorming",
      "superpowers/writing-plans"
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Card 410: copy several catalogue skills into ~/.spectro/skills in one request, all or nothing. Every id is checked before anything is written; one unknown or already carried id refuses the whole set with 409 and a refused list naming each id with status, message, name and root. A copy that fails after others landed deletes those again and answers 413 or 500 with the failing id; a copy that will not delete stays and the answer is 500 with those ids under leftover. 400 no list. Answers {installed:[{skill,name,pack,files,bytes,licence,commit}]}.
  
  Body: {skills: ["<pack>/<name>", ...]}: ids from the catalogue rows of GET /api/skills.
  
  CAUTION: Copies files into ~/.spectro/skills. It never overwrites; one taken name refuses the whole set.
  
  Fence: host+origin+json — Loopback fence plus Origin check, and the request must carry Content-Type: application/json — anything else is 415.
  
  Writes state: yes
}
